A||||7||ezsurf||Right Turn Signal||||5||
Z||000000||ezsurf||12-12-2000||11:43 PM||||I've got a little problem with my right turn signal. When I position the turn stalk to indicate a right turn, the light comes on but does not flash.  Neither the indicator light on the instrument panel nor the turn signal light itself flashes.  I could use some help on this one.  Does this sound like a turn signal relay problem, or a problem with the turn stalk?  Any electrical experts out there?  TIA - ez.||||reg||5
Z||000001||RNGCRSH||12-13-2000||01:52 AM||||Are both the front and rear exterior turn signal bulbs good? I dont know if this applies, but I had an old dodge, and if a bulb was out the other would not flash. The relay worked on heat generated by the current going to both bulbs if there was only one bulb it would not get hot enough for the relay to cycle/flash.<p>[This message has been edited by RNGCRSH (edited 12-13-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Elenor84||12-13-2000||01:59 AM||||This happened to me like a month ago...trust me nothing is wrong with any relays...wen u singnal right your signal light at the back comes on right?  Wrong...that is just your break light...your right signal light is burnt out!  Thas all it is!  a 40cent part!  Take the covers off and tell me if I'm wrong...<P>Lance<BR>||||reg||10
Z||000003||Standard||12-13-2000||05:44 AM||||My GT did that when I bought it, except it was the left.  The turn indicator stayed on all the time, and the turn signals didn't blink, they just stayed on.  The whole problem was the weather pack for the connector on the front turn signal wasn't pushed into the socket, so the connector wasn't making full contact with the bulb..<P>found the thread to read:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20001206-2-003863.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20001206-2-003863.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||ThatRickGuy||12-13-2000||10:38 AM||||most of the time, turn signals will fail 1 of 2 ways. Once you turn the signal selector...<P>1. Turn light on dash comes on, lights are dead, no blinking. Solution: Bad connection or dead turn signal light.<P>2. No light on dash, turn lights will either be dead, or stuck on. Solution: Bad Relay, costs like $3 at napa, silver cylinder with either 2 or 3 prongs (haven't checked the fiero's yet) there are 2 of these on your car, 1 for your turn signals, and one for your hazards, make sure you replace the correct one.||||reg||1
Z||000005||StuGood||12-13-2000||12:40 PM||||Everytime you need to turn right, just roll down the window and use hand signal.  That, or just turn left thrice.<P>Corny, true, but not too for Stu  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ||||reg||12
Z||000006||ezsurf||12-13-2000||10:48 PM||||Thanks for the input.  I need to get some help to check the bulbs, can't check it by myself.  The last time I drove it a cop pulled up behind me at a stop sign.  I was going to turn right, but I quickly decided to turn left instead.  I'll check the bulbs first, then the connections.  If that doesn't fix it, I'll see how the relays look.  It's nice to know the relays  don't cost $30 like everything else on this car.  Sure wish it was summer again, it ought to be against the law to work on a car in cold weather.||||reg||1
Z||000007||ezsurf||12-13-2000||10:57 PM||||OOps!  Had a small brain **** there.  I was thinking I was checking the brake lights, don't need help checking the turn signals. As Gilda Radnor would say, - nevermind.||||reg||1
